+RE4 JPN RNG Tracer for Dolphin
+================================
+
+Target
+------
+Game ID: G4BJ08 (Biohazard 4 JPN)
+RNG function: 0x8014BDA0
+Global 16-bit RNG state: 0x802B69BC
+
+What this patch does
+--------------------
+1. Captures the exact GameCube controller state delivered to controller 1.
+2. Hooks execution of 0x8014BDA0 in the x86-64 JIT and in the Interpreter.
+3. For every RNG call, records:
+   - global call index
+   - movie frame
+   - Dolphin input count
+   - controller poll index
+   - call number inside that poll
+   - caller (LR - 4)
+   - LR
+   - seed before
+   - predicted seed after
+   - RNG output byte
+   - buttons and all analog controller fields
+4. Displays a small cyan OSD status line with the previous poll's RNG call count,
+   total calls, last caller, seed transition, and current controller state.
+5. Writes a CSV trace to:
+   <Dolphin User Folder>/Logs/re4_jpn_rng_trace.csv
+
+Important
+---------
+The "seed_after" column is calculated from the RE4 JPN RNG transformation that
+was previously validated against the Japanese main.dol. The real seed_before
+is read directly from emulated memory at 0x802B69BC on every call.
+
+The hook is active only for game ID G4BJ08.
+
+CPU cores
+---------
+- x86-64 JIT: supported (the normal Windows x64 Dolphin path)
+- Interpreter: supported
+- Cached Interpreter / ARM64 JIT: not instrumented by this patch
+
+Files changed
+-------------
+Source/Core/Core/RE4RNGTrace.cpp        (new)
+Source/Core/Core/RE4RNGTrace.h          (new)
+Source/Core/Core/Movie.cpp
+Source/Core/Core/PowerPC/Jit64/Jit.cpp
+Source/Core/Core/PowerPC/Interpreter/Interpreter.cpp
+Source/Core/Core/CMakeLists.txt
+Source/Core/VideoCommon/OnScreenDisplay.h
+
+About this ZIP
+--------------
+The GitHub source ZIP supplied for patching does not contain the contents of
+Dolphin's git submodules. A complete build therefore needs either:
+
+  git clone --recursive https://github.com/dolphin-emu/dolphin.git
+
+or a checkout where the submodules have already been initialized. The included
+RE4_JPN_RNG_TRACER.patch can be applied to such a checkout.
+
+Expected use for the TAS investigation
+--------------------------------------
+Run the optimized incendiary baseline and save re4_jpn_rng_trace.csv.
+Then run a movie/input variation and save its CSV separately. Comparing the two
+traces shows the first poll/caller where the RNG agenda diverges, which is the
+key information needed to map input changes to RNG consumption without GDB.
